{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1789136288","published":"2026-09-11T14:18:18Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:43:18.336085508Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-59858","CVE-2026-73073"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-73073","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: Arbitrary Ex command execution during C omni-completion: s:StructMembers() in runtime/autoload/ccomplete.vim interpolates a tags-file typeref/typename value into a :vimgrep pattern with only \"/\" and \"\\\" escaped, so an unclosed \"[\" makes vimgrep pattern skipping fail and a following \"|\" is then parsed as an Ex command separator, running the rest of the tag value as Ex commands\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-73073.patch: match the typename literally in s:StructMembers() by prefixing it with \"\\V\" and restoring magic mode with \"\\m\" for the trailing \"\\(\\t\\|$\\)\" group, so no regex metacharacter in the tag field can affect :vimgrep pattern parsing; this completes CVE-2026-59858.patch (upstream 9.2.0735), whose escaping alone was insufficient; the upstream src/version.c bump and the new src/testdir/test_plugin_ccomplete.vim test are omitted as they do not apply to 8.1.0875\n     - CVE-2026-73073","affected":[{"package":{"name":"vim","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/vim?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:8.1.0875-5+deb10u6+tuxcare.els28"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1789136288.json"}},{"package":{"name":"vim-athena","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/vim-athena?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:8.1.0875-5+deb10u6+tuxcare.els28"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1789136288.json"}},{"package":{"name":"vim-common","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/vim-common?d